export abstract anchor SpecWriting:
    workingWithPiton:
        Read piton.config.pi to find the source root, the entry, the
        output, the plugins and the adapters. Then read the entry and its
        index files to the anchors of the task. The compiled reference
        gives an overview. If it does not agree with the source, the
        source is correct.

        Read the related source before you change it. Do not edit
        generated output. This includes generated guidance files, skill,
        command and agent files, renderer output, and files in
        .piton/manifest.json. Make each change in the .pi source, then
        build again.

        Open a reference only when the work needs it. Use piton reach to
        find what a change can affect. Use piton slice to read only the
        spec that one anchor or property needs.

        Make the smallest change that does the task. Use the conventions
        of the files near it. Then run piton format and piton check, and
        fix each problem in the source. Run piton build and read the diff
        of the generated files. Report each compiler error and warning as
        it is, with its file. Do not report success that the compiler
        did not show.

    specProse:
        Write the prose of a specification in ASD-STE100 Simplified
        Technical English. Keep the structure that the specification
        needs. Put prose in string blocks, and put structure in keys and
        lists.

    specOrganization:
        - Put one exported anchor in each file. Give the file the name of the anchor.
        - Put related files in one folder. Give each folder an index.pi with from ./X export * for each file.
        - Make a new folder when a topic has more than one file, or when a folder holds unrelated topics.
        - Make sure that the entry reaches each new file through the index files.
        - Use the words of the user for names. Anchor names are UpperCamelCase. Property names are lowerCamelCase.
        - Use \ @{X} \ to refer to an anchor. Do not copy its content.

    specInheritance:
        - Use inheritance when two or more anchors share properties.
        - Put the shared properties in an abstract base. Put shared bases in a lib folder.
        - Do not make a base for only one anchor.
        - Give an abstract base a keyword when many anchors implement it.
        - Keep each inheritance chain short.
